Dear Mr. Garvey,<br />
<br />
The firm's response to your November 14 letter is attached, together with a=
 production of the underlying documents: the ten emails from the 2011 matte=
r sequence recovered from the firm's mail journal archive, with their attac=
hments, and the October 2013 audit-response correspondence.<br />
<br />
The short of it: on June 9, 2011, Torvane's General Counsel confirmed in wr=
iting, by email and by signed letter, that the warranty claim against Brand=
t Thermal Systems was expressly outside Prescott Vane's engagement; that To=
rvane had elected not to assert it after this firm identified the claim, an=
alyzed the limitations period, recommended a tolling agreement, and advised=
 in writing that the claim would likely become time-barred; and that the co=
nfirmation stood unless withdrawn in writing. It never was. In October 2013=
, your client's same General Counsel enforced that limitation herself, dire=
cting that the Brandt matter be removed from this firm's audit response to =
Caulfield Roth "as I confirmed to Arthur in writing on June 9, 2011" - her =
words, twenty-eight months later.<br />
<br />
The premise of your letter - that the firm was engaged on the Brandt claim =
and stood silent while it expired - is refuted by your client's own documen=
ts. We invite the claim's withdrawal within thirty days, failing which the =
firm will respond formally through counsel and will seek every available re=
medy for a claim pursued against this record.<br />
<br />
Evelyn Stanhope<br />
General Counsel<br />
Prescott Vane LLP
